ckground is the dominant color. - One non-background color forms a full solid row and a full solid column,   splitting the grid into four nonempty quadrants. - Each quadrant contains exactly one single-color sprite on the background;   each sprite has a 3x3 tight bounding box.  Rule - Remove the separator row and column. - In each quadrant, crop the sprite to its tight bounding box, preserving   background holes inside the crop. - Concatenate the four crops in quadrant order: upper-left, upper-right,   lower-left, lower-right.  Key insight - The cross is only a layout divider; the output is a compact atlas of the   four local sprites in their original relative quadrant positions. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "transform_in_place",   "src": "grid divided into four regions by a solid one-pixel separator cross, with one 3x3-bbox sprite in each region",   "transform": "remove the separator cross; crop each sprite to its tight bbox and concatenate the crops in upper-left, upper-right, lower-left, lower-right quadrant order",   "grid_shape": "6x6 montage of four 3x3 sprite crops" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="5" source="train" puzzle_id="b548a754"> <similarity> score=0.2520 mechanism=0.0000 lexical=0.0000 code_feature=0.6000 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/b548a754.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b548a754.json </paths> <description> Stretch the colored rectangular frame outward until its far edge reaches the lone marker pixel.  Input structure - The background is the most common color. - A single marker pixel is the only foreground color that appears once. - All other foreground pixels form one solid rectangular frame with one border color and one interior color.  Rule - If the marker is above or below the frame and its column lies within the frame, extend the frame vertically to the marker row. - If the marker is left or right of the frame and its row lies within