r sprites separated by a solid cross and pack them into a 2x2 montage.  Input structure - The background is the dominant color. - One non-background color forms a full solid row and a full solid column,   splitting the grid into four nonempty quadrants. - Each quadrant contains exactly one single-color sprite on the background;   each sprite has a 3x3 tight bounding box.  Rule - Remove the separator row and column. - In each quadrant, crop the sprite to its tight bounding box, preserving   background holes inside the crop. - Concatenate the four crops in quadrant order: upper-left, upper-right,   lower-left, lower-right.  Key insight - The cross is only a layout divider; the output is a compact atlas of the   four local sprites in their original relative quadrant positions. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "transform_in_place",   "src": "grid divided into four regions by a solid one-pixel separator cross, with one 3x3-bbox sprite in each region",   "transform": "remove the separator cross; crop each sprite to its tight bbox and concatenate the crops in upper-left, upper-right, lower-left, lower-right quadrant order",   "grid_shape": "6x6 montage of four 3x3 sprite crops" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="5" source="train" puzzle_id="b548a754"> <similarity> score=0.2520 mechanism=0.0000 lexical=0.0000 code_feature=0.6000 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/b548a754.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b548a754.json </paths> <description> Stretch the colored rectangular frame outward until its far edge reaches the lone marker pixel.  Input structure - The background is the most common color. - A single marker pixel is the only foreground color that appears once. - All other foreground pixels form one solid rectangular frame with one border color and one interior color.  Rule - If the marker is above or below the frame and its column lies within the frame, extend the frame vertically to the marker row. - If the marker is left or right of the frame and its row lies within the frame, extend the frame horizontally to the marker column. - Redraw the expanded rectangle with the same border and interior colors; everything outside remains background.  Key insight The marker selects which side of the rectangle moves and where the new outer border lies; it is consumed by that border. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "transform_in_place",   "src": "one two-color rectangular frame on the background plus a singleton marker pixel aligned with one side span",   "transform": "erase the marker and redraw the frame expanded in the marker direction so the marker row or column becomes the new outer border; preserve the frame border and interior colors" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="6" source="train" puzzle_id="b2862040"> <similarity> score=0.2421 mechanism=0.0000 lexical=0.0104 code_feature=0.5000 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/b2862040.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b2862040.json </paths> <description> Recolor every foreground object that encloses a background hole to teal.  Input structure - The grid has one dominant background color and exactly one foreground color. - The foreground pixels form separate 4-connected objects. - Teal is absent from the input and is reserved as the output mark.  Rule - Keep objects whose bbox contains no enclosed background region unchanged. - For each foreground object with a 4-connected background hole inside its bbox, recolor all of that object's pixels to teal. - Leave background pixels unchanged, including the holes themselves.  Key insight - The changed objects are selected by topology, not by size or position: they are precisely the objects whose mask has an interior hole. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "transform_in_place",   "src": "single-color 4-connected foreground objects on a background; some objects enclose background holes",   "transform": "recolor each object that encloses a 4-connected background hole to teal; preserve objects without holes and all background pixels" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="7" source="train" puzzle_id="3ad05f52"> <similarity> score=0.2314 mechanism=0.0000 lexical=0.0000 code_feature=0.4286 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3ad05f52.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3ad05f52.json </paths> <description> Paint the maze corridor and framed rooms lying on shortest paths between the two colored endpoint components.  Input structure - The grid has a dominant background, one wall color forming thin orthogonal frames, and one endpoint/fill color. - The endpoint/fill color forms exactly two 4-connected solid rectangular components; their larger side lengths define the framed room sizes.  Rule - Treat wall pixels as blocked and every other pixel as passable. - Find every passable pixel that lies on a shortest 4-connected path between the two endpoint components. - Also fill any framed square room of an endpoint-derived size that intersects that shortest-path mask.  Key insight - Shortest paths identify the route through open connector corridors, while the wall-bordered square rooms need to be expanded from the route centerline to their full interior. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "move_along_path",   "src": "one of two same-color endpoint components",   "dst": "the other same-color endpoint component",   "path": "shortest 4-connected route through non-wall pixels",   "trajectory": "paint background pixels on the route with the endpoint color",   "transform": "fill any wall-framed square room of an endpoint-derived size that the route crosses" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="8" source="train" puzzle_id="8efcae92"> <similarity> score=0.2520 mechanism=0.0000 lexical=0.0000 code_feature=0.6000 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/8efcae92.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8efcae92.json </paths> <description> Crop out the foreground rectangle that contains the most marker pixels.  Input structure - The upper-left cell is background. - The foreground consists of multiple 4-connected solid rectangles made from   a common fill color, with a rarer marker color replacing some cells.  Rule - Treat the rarer of the two foreground colors as the marker color. - Count marker pixels inside each foreground rectangle. - Return the exact bounding-box crop of the unique rectangle with the largest   marker count.  Key insight - The output is not redrawn or recolored; it is one existing input rectangle   selected by the count of its marker pixels. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "transform_in_place",   "src": "solid foreground rectangles containing sparse marker pixels",   "transform": "select the rectangle with the largest marker-pixel count and return it unchanged",   "grid_shape": "tight crop to the selected rectangle bbox" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  ## 必读参考代码路径  执行前请至少快速阅读这些文件的 `main()` 和 `generate_input()`，重点看它们如何避免退化输入、如何随机放置对象、如何验证隐式假设：  - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2601afb7.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/62593bfd.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/afe3afe9.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/0bb8deee.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/b548a754.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/b2862040.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3ad05f52.py` - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/8efcae92.py`  ## 公共参考工具箱  执行前还必须快速阅读 `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/solvers/arc_utils.py`。它是 ARC 公共工具箱，包含统一的 `(r, c)` 坐标约定、bbox、连通域、裁剪、几何变换、颜色和网格操作等公共实现。生成代码时优先参考或复用这些函数；若直接 import，请确保目标文件仍可被 `SourceFileLoader` 直接加载，自检命令能独立运行。  ## 实现要求  1. `main(grid)` 必须实现新题描述中的确定性转换规则，不能只识别 `generate_input()` 的固定模板。禁止不同的input网格输出相同的output网格。 2. `generate_input()` 必须随机生成多样样例，不能固定死。随机维度应覆盖：网格大小、对象数量、位置、颜色、方向、形状参数或关键分支。注意若描述中存在若干，需实现而不是只有单个，包括object或者对应关系等等。 3. 生成器必须保证输入满足 `main()` 的隐式假设：对象不重叠、不越界、特殊标记唯一或可区分、匹配关系无歧义、关键分支出现概率相同。 4. 禁止把 ARC 颜色 id 、亮度、拼写等当作人类不可见的数值语义参与排序、大小比较或隐藏映射。颜色变化必须有可见结构线索。注意颜色亮度、拼写等也是不可见信息，若描述中出现违规的颜色id或者亮度，可自行使用少量的固定颜色替代，但注意生成时要在三个以内输入输出网格中对所有变换100%覆盖度。 5. 输出样例要视觉清晰，人类必须能从输入输出对中肉眼辨认出规律。具体要求：避免对象粘连、覆盖关系混乱、同一像素多重语义；不同逻辑步骤产生的结果不要大面积层叠在一起导致无法分辨哪个颜色属于哪个步骤；输入中各元素之间保持足够间距，输出中新增的标记/填充/路径等应与背景和已有元素在颜色上有明显区分；若规则涉及多层叠加，生成时控制对象密度和尺寸，确保叠加区域只占少数像素而非铺满整个网格。 6. 若规则有多个分支，生成器不能长期固定成一个分支；应让分支在随机样例中合理出现。分支概率不必平均——难以发现的隐蔽分支（如少数情况下才触发的特殊规则）应适当提高出现概率，确保在 3 个训练示例中至少出现一次，否则求解者无法归纳该规则。对于颜色映射类规则，确保 2 个左右的示例即可覆盖所有映射关系（每种颜色→颜色的映射至少在某个示例中出现过）。 7. 代码风格参考 `ARC_code`：使用 `numpy`，并把 `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/solvers/arc_utils.py` 作为公共参考工具箱，优先复用其中已经稳定的 bbox、连通域、裁剪、变换和颜色工具；目标文件必须能被 `SourceFileLoader` 直接加载。 8. 可以在目标目录放公共 helper 文件，或从 `arc_utils.py` 摘取少量必要函数；若只实现一道题，优先保持目标文件自包含，减少额外依赖。 9. `main(grid)` 必须带一段 docstring，按 `ARC_code` 参考题的格式分四部分书写：首行用一句话概述转换目标；随后 `Input structure:` 描述输入网格中的对象/背景/标记/边界/组件；`Rule:` 给出从输入到输出的确定性变换规则；`Key insight:` 点明解题核心洞见。该 docstring 供下游相似度/索引流程（按 `main` 的 docstring 抽取机制标签）使用，缺失会导致此题无法被收录为参考题。 10. 网格尺寸必须符合 ARC 规范：`generate_input()` 产生的输入网格、以及 `main()` 返回的输出网格，行数和列数都必须 ≤ 30（即任何一维都不超过 30，整体不超过 30×30）。随机化网格大小时把上界封顶在 30；若规则会放大网格（如平铺、加边框、整数倍缩放），必须保证放大后的输出仍 ≤ 30×30，必要时收紧输入尺寸或放大倍数的随机范围，确保 100% 的随机样例都不越过 30×30。  ## 写入要求  将完整代码写入：  `/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/7/027/3.py`  默认使用 `.py` 后缀，便于编辑器、lint 和 Python 工具识别；如果调用方传入空后缀，则按无扩展名文件写入。  ## 自检要求  写完后必须运行类似下面的验证，并修复失败：  ```bash python - <<'PY' from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader from pathlib import Path import hashlib import numpy as np  p = Path("/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/7/027/3.py") mod = SourceFileLoader("new_arc_task", str(p)).load_module() sigs = set() for i in range(100):     inp = mod.generate_input()     out = mod.main(inp)     assert isinstance(inp, np.ndarray)     assert isinstance(out, np.ndarray)     assert inp.ndim == 2 and max(inp.shape) <= 30, f"input grid exceeds 30x30: {inp.shape}"     assert out.ndim == 2 and max(out.shape) <= 30, f"output grid exceeds 30x30: {out.shape}"     sigs.add(hashlib.md5(inp.tobytes() + str(inp.shape).encode()).hexdigest()) print("variants", len(sigs)) assert len(sigs) >= 20 PY python -m py_compile "/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/7/027/3.py" ```  最后清理验证产生的 `__pycache__`。 
