background is the most common color. - One non-background color forms complete horizontal and vertical divider   lines, partitioning the grid into rectangular cells. - Every occupied cell away from the dividers contains pixels of exactly one   non-background, non-divider color. - For each sprite color, occupied cells occur as connected three-cell groups   inside a 2-by-2 block of equal-sized cells.  Rule: - Split the grid at the divider rows and columns. - For each three-cell monochrome group in a 2-by-2 cell block, find the one   empty cell in that block. - Reflect each of the three present cell-local sprites vertically and/or   horizontally according to its relative position to the missing cell; all   three reflections must produce the same mask. - Paint that agreed reflected sprite into the missing cell, leaving dividers   and all existing cells unchanged.  Key insight: - The sprites are mirror variants around the center of a 2-by-2 block of   lattice cells, so any three visible variants uniquely determine the fourth. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "symmetry/pattern",   "src": "monochrome sprites occupying three cells of a 2x2 block in the divider-line lattice",   "dst": "empty fourth cell of each same-color 2x2 block",   "transform": "reflect the present cell-local sprite masks horizontally and/or vertically around the 2x2 block center; paint the unique agreed reflected sprite into the empty cell and preserve the lattice" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="5" source="train" puzzle_id="52364a65"> <similarity> score=1.0609 mechanism=1.0000 lexical=0.0047 code_feature=0.5000 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/52364a65.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/52364a65.json </paths> <description> Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.  Input structure: - A grid has one dominant background color and several monochroma